From 54c0044f35a4f4f19aaf4e6eb1794e266c3115bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:13:26 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] power: 8916: boost from kiwi's performance profile

Replace the perfd interaction and launch boosts with our own, driven by
the profile picked in Settings > System > Performance. init sets the
CPU touch floors through the kernel's cpu_boost and leaves the rest of
the profile in vendor.kiwi.perf.*.

On a touch, wake the parked fast cores and put a floor under the GPU
clock. An app launch also holds both clusters near their top clock
through msm_performance. Everything is let go once the last request
runs out, and the Stock profile turns it all off.
---
